From d739a5e2b1499f67a668e21add59e4c12f88a187 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:14:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): reconcile_notify supervisor op runs
 receipt-gated reconcile_refused_sub outside the worker fence [daveey]

A Kanban worker cannot run kanban_notify_reconcile.reconcile_refused_sub: every
worker subprocess is write-fenced. It now files kanban_supervisor_request op
{op: reconcile_notify, task_id, chat_id, thread_id?} (no evidence fields) and the
non-worker executor (dispatcher tick / supervisor-requests --drain) runs it.

hermes_cli/kanban_notify_reconcile_exec.py reads the evidence itself from the
owner gateway: a hermes-hub notice-receipts request (client >= 1.9.24) against the
owner's own session store, for the exact pending remote:<gw>:<profile>/<board>/
<task>:<event> keys; candidate owner from the task's hub subscription. Phase 1
mints and queues one read per (gw, profile, chat) and parks the request in phase
awaiting_owner; phase 2 polls hub.db sent rows each drain without spending
delivery attempts. Only a done answer whose envelope and echo match backs the
unchanged reconcile_refused_sub; every other outcome (no receipt, unknown owner,
unreadable local store, local chat, owner read failed, owner silent 24 h,
mismatch, new completion since the read) keeps the row. Never sends, wakes or
moves cursors. Results land as supervisor_request_* event + comment.

Kanban t_01a190436c055e7d.
